   "created_utc": "2020-07-25T11:05:39Z",
   "last_edit_utc": null,
   "last_activity_utc": "2020-07-25T11:05:39Z",
   "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
   "body_html": "<p>valgrind provides various ways to track memory allocations that are later on deallocated.</p>\n<p>To see peak of memory, you can e.g. use the valgrind massif tool.</p>\n<p>To see which code allocates/deallocates a lot of memory, you can e.g. use memcheck option --xtree-memory=full and visualise the resulting file with kcachegrind.</p>\n"
  }
